{"id":"deuten","lemma":"deuten","pos":"verb","rank":4269,"glosses":["to interpret (e.g. dreams), to understand, to read (e.g. signs)","to point [with auf (+ accusative) ‘at something’], to indicate","to suggest, point towards"],"ipa":"/ˈdɔʏ̯tən/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/01/De-deuten.ogg/De-deuten.ogg.mp3","conjugation":{"indicative":{"present":{"1s":"deute","1p":"deuten","2s":"deutest","2p":"deutet","3s":"deutet","3p":"deuten"},"preterite":{"1s":"deutete","1p":"deuteten","2s":"deutetest","2p":"deutetet","3s":"deutete","3p":"deuteten"},"perfect":{"1s":"habe gedeutet","1p":"haben gedeutet","2s":"hast gedeutet","2p":"habt gedeutet","3s":"hat gedeutet","3p":"haben gedeutet"},"future":{"1s":"werde deuten","1p":"werden deuten","2s":"wirst deuten","2p":"werdet deuten","3s":"wird deuten","3p":"werden deuten"}},"imperative":{"affirmative":{"2s":"deut","2p":"deutet"}},"subjunctive":{"conditional":{"1s":"würde deuten","1p":"würden deuten","2s":"würdest deuten","2p":"würdet deuten","3s":"würde deuten","3p":"würden deuten"}}},"nonFinite":{"participle":"gedeutet"},"examples":[{"text":"Alles deutet auf seine Schuld.","en":"Everything points to his guilt.","words":[{"g":"everything"},null,{"g":"on"},{"g":"his","l":"seiner"},{"g":"debt"}]},{"text":"Was deutest du an?","en":"What are you implying?","words":[{"g":"what"},null,{"g":"you"},{"g":"at / on"}]},{"text":"Ich weiß nicht, wie ich seine Worte deuten soll.","en":"I don't know how to interpret his words.","words":[{"g":"I"},{"g":"to know","l":"wissen"},{"g":"not"},{"g":"how"},{"g":"I"},{"g":"his","l":"seiner"},{"g":"word as an isolated unit","l":"Wort"},null,{"g":"should","l":"sollen"}]},{"text":"Sie deutete an, dass das Problem ernst sei.","en":"She indicated that the problem was serious.","words":[{"g":"she / they / you"},null,{"g":"at / on"},{"g":"that"},{"g":"the / that"},{"g":"problem"},{"g":"serious, severe, grave"},{"g":"to be","l":"sein"}]},{"text":"Er deutete mein Schweigen als Zustimmung.","en":"He interpreted my silence as consent.","words":[{"g":"he / it"},null,{"g":"my"},{"g":"silence"},{"g":"at the same moment"},{"g":"agreement"}]}]}